# Development and CI tooling for Darwin's advisory quality gates (P0.2). This file
# is the SOURCE you edit; requirements-dev.txt is the generated, hash-locked
# closure (runtime + dev tools + transitive, with --generate-hashes) and is never
# hand-edited. It is what CI installs with --require-hashes.
#
# Includes the runtime requirements (via -r requirements.in) plus the dev tools.
# Each dev tool is pinned to the stable version resolved at authoring time
# (2026-06-14; cyclonedx-bom and pip-audit added 2026-06-17). All quality gates
# are advisory in CI (.github/workflows/quality.yml); coverage is reported, not
# gated (.github/workflows/ci.yml). Current baseline finding counts are recorded
# in docs/quality-baseline.md. The blocking flip is P7.2.
#
# Regenerate on Python 3.13:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements-dev.txt requirements-dev.in
-r requirements.in
ruff==0.15.17
mypy==2.1.0
pytest-cov==7.1.0
# Supply-chain CI tooling (P6.2.2), both pip-ecosystem to match pip-tools:
# cyclonedx-bom provides the cyclonedx-py SBOM generator (the sbom job in ci.yml);
# pip-audit is the advisory dependency vulnerability scanner (the vuln-scan job in
# quality.yml). Dev/CI tools only; they do not enter the runtime lock. See
# decision 0029.
cyclonedx-bom==7.3.1
pip-audit==2.10.1
